<p class="legal-updated">Last updated: 1 November 2026</p>
<p>This Privacy Policy explains how the Infrastructure Concession Regulatory Commission (“ICRC”, “we”, “us”) collects, uses and protects personal information through the ICRC SCODEX 2026 portal (the “Portal”) for the 2026 staff orientation programme (the “Programme”). We process personal information in line with the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023.</p>

<h3>1. Who is responsible for your information</h3>
<p>ICRC is the data controller for personal information processed through the Portal. The Portal is used only to run the Programme for newly recruited staff, facilitators and authorised programme personnel.</p>

<h3>2. Information we collect</h3>
<p><strong>Account and contact details.</strong> Your name (including any middle or preferred name), email address and phone number. Facilitators may also provide an organisation, title and alternative phone number.</p>
<p><strong>Job details.</strong> Staff number, department, designation, programme group, resumption date and duty location, usually assigned by ICRC.</p>
<p><strong>Orientation details.</strong> Accommodation information and any programme-specific information requested on the activation form.</p>
<p><strong>Person to contact in an emergency.</strong> Their name, relationship to you and phone number. These fields are optional unless the Programme requires them.</p>
<p><strong>Photograph.</strong> An optional profile photo, used on your programme badge and profile.</p>
<p><strong>Attendance records.</strong> Your daily sign-in and sign-out times, punctuality, duration and the method used. Depending on the method:</p>
<ul>
<li><em>Device sign-in:</em> a security credential for your registered device (a public key and device label). Your fingerprint, face or device PIN never leaves your device and is never sent to or stored by ICRC. We also record your location at the moment of sign-in and sign-out to confirm you are within the approved venue.</li>
<li><em>Badge scanner:</em> the badge scanned and the authorised operator who scanned it.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Learning records.</strong> Assessment answers and attempts, assignment and presentation submissions (including uploaded files), scores, facilitator feedback and Session Q&amp;A questions.</p>
<p><strong>Technical and security information.</strong> Your IP address, browser details and session information when you use the Portal, security logs of attendance actions, and audit records of significant account and administrative actions. When you activate your account, Google reCAPTCHA may be used to confirm that you are not an automated program.</p>
<p>We do not ask for bank details or national identity numbers through the Portal.</p>

<h3>3. How we use your information</h3>
<ul>
<li>to create and manage your account and control access to the Portal;</li>
<li>to run the Programme: timetables, learning materials, announcements, assessments and feedback;</li>
<li>to record and verify daily attendance and report on attendance and progress;</li>
<li>to produce programme badges;</li>
<li>to send Programme emails, such as invitations, password resets, announcements, newly assigned work and released results;</li>
<li>to contact your emergency contact if there is an emergency;</li>
<li>to keep the Portal secure, prevent misuse and investigate problems.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do not sell your information, use it for advertising, or make decisions about you based solely on automated processing. Objective quiz answers are marked automatically, but results are released by facilitators, and written work is reviewed by people.</p>

<h3>4. Our lawful basis</h3>
<p>We process your information because it is necessary to onboard and develop ICRC staff, which is part of your employment relationship with ICRC and of our functions as a public body. We also rely on our legitimate interest in running a secure and fair programme, and on legal obligations where they apply. Where information is optional, such as a profile photo, providing it is your choice.</p>

<h3>5. Who can see your information</h3>
<p>Access is role based and limited to what each person needs:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>You</strong> can see your own profile, attendance, submissions and released results.</li>
<li><strong>ICRC programme administrators</strong> can see and manage participant records.</li>
<li><strong>Facilitators and supervisors</strong> can see only the areas they have been authorised for, such as attendance, assessments or Q&amp;A.</li>
<li><strong>Other participants</strong> can see Session Q&amp;A questions and answers only after a moderator publishes them. Your badge, which shows your name, photo and programme details, is visible to anyone who sees you wear it.</li>
</ul>
<p>Your exact location coordinates are not shown in attendance reports or exports. We share information outside ICRC only with service providers that help us operate the Portal, such as hosting, email delivery and Google reCAPTCHA, or where the law requires it.</p>

<h3>6. How we protect your information</h3>
<p>Personal profile details, including accommodation and emergency contact information, and attendance location data are encrypted when stored. Uploaded photos and files are stored privately and served only to authorised users. Passwords are stored in hashed form, sessions expire after a period of inactivity, and significant actions are recorded in audit logs. No system is completely secure, so please protect your password and device.</p>

<h3>7. How long we keep your information</h3>
<p>We keep Programme records for as long as they are needed to run the Programme and to meet ICRC’s administrative, staff-record and legal obligations. After that, they are deleted or anonymised in line with ICRC’s records retention policy.</p>

<h3>8. Your rights</h3>
<p>Under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 you may ask to access the personal information we hold about you, correct inaccurate information, object to or restrict certain processing, request deletion where we have no need to keep it, and receive a copy of information you provided. You can update permitted personal details from your profile at any time. For anything else, contact your programme administrator. If you are not satisfied with our response, you may complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission.</p>

<h3>9. Cookies</h3>
<p>The Portal uses only essential cookies, to keep you signed in and to protect forms from forgery. We do not use advertising or analytics cookies. If Google reCAPTCHA is shown on the activation form, Google may set its own cookies under its privacy policy.</p>

<h3>10. Changes to this policy</h3>
<p>We may update this policy when the Programme or the Portal changes. The date at the top shows when it was last updated.</p>

<h3>11. Contact</h3>
<p>For questions about this policy or your information, contact your programme facilitator or administrator, or use the Support section of this site. Please also read the <a href="{{ url('/terms') }}" data-legal-open="terms">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.</p>
